<title>TURKEY: Turk Petrol Ofisi H1 profit up 82.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Petrol Ofisi H1 profit up 82.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>				    H1 1997	   H1 1996</p>
<p>				    -------	   -------</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira) 7,279.24  vs   3,981.76</p>
<p>    Net profit		  1,039.96  vs   1,580.06</p>
<p>    Net sales		 211,846.67  vs 119,835.29</p>
<p>    Operating profit	 12,546.91  vs   6,278.27</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	7,245.51  vs   3,494.03</p>
<p>    Interest paid		   0     vs	0</p>
<p>    Total debts		32,237.76  vs  15,295.65</p>
<p>    Equity		     21,576.08  vs   9,523.55</p>
<p>    Capital		     7,000.00  vs   2,520.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkish petroleum products marketer and lubricants producer Petrol Ofisi A.S. is slated for privatisation with 93.3 percent of its capital held by the privatisation body OIB.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
